  "description": "Copies Microsoft's DirectX Shader Compiler (dxcompiler.dll, dxil.dll) into the application's output on win-x64, where SharpSlang loads it for Slang, so Slang can emit DXIL for D3D12. Carries no binary: depends on Microsoft.Direct3D.DXC at a pinned version, copies the two DLLs from it, and fails the build when another version is restored (SHARPSLANG011). Optional: without it SharpSlang compiles SPIR-V only.",
